-- title:
--   Theorem 2 — EGRAAL converges to a solution of a monotone variational inequality
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal E$ be a finite-dimensional real inner product space, $g:\mathcal E\to(-\infty,+\infty]$ and $F:\operatorname{dom} g\to\mathcal E$, and assume:
--
--   1. (C1) the solution set $S$ of the variational inequality $\langle F(z^*),z-z^*\rangle+g(z)-g(z^*)\ge0$ for all $z\in\mathcal E$ is nonempty;
--   2. (C2) $g$ is proper, convex and lower semicontinuous;
--   3. (C3) $F$ is monotone on $\operatorname{dom} g$;
--   4. $F$ is locally Lipschitz continuous, in the form: Lipschitz on every bounded subset of $\operatorname{dom} g$.
--
--   Let $(z^k)$, $(\bar z^k)$ be generated by Algorithm 1 (the Explicit Golden Ratio Algorithm) with any $\phi\in(1,\varphi]$, $\bar\lambda>0$, $\lambda_0>0$ and any starting points $z^0,z^1$. Then there is $z^*\in S$ with
--   $$z^k\to z^* \quad\text{and}\quad \bar z^k\to z^*\qquad (k\to\infty).$$
--
--   The theorem shows that a method with fully explicit, adaptive stepsizes — no linesearch and no knowledge of a Lipschitz constant — solves monotone variational inequalities with a merely locally Lipschitz operator.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper's "locally Lipschitz" is formalized as Lipschitz continuity on every bounded subset of $\operatorname{dom} g$, the property its proof (via Lemma 2) uses; the two agree when $\operatorname{dom} g$ is closed and the formal hypothesis is stronger otherwise. $F$ is a total map whose values off $\operatorname{dom} g$ are never used.
-- source:
--   Malitsky, Golden Ratio Algorithms for Variational Inequalities, preprint (Optimization Online 6598, 2018), p. 6, Theorem 2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_Explicit_viProblem
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_Explicit_egraalRun
open Filter Topology

namespace GoldenRatioVI.Explicit

/-- Theorem 2 of Malitsky (p. 6): suppose that `F` is locally Lipschitz continuous (here: Lipschitz
on every bounded subset of `dom g`) and conditions (C1)–(C3) hold. Then the sequences `(z^k)` and
`(z̄^k)` generated by Algorithm 1 (EGRAAL) converge to a common solution of the variational
inequality (1). -/
theorem egraal_converges {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (g : E → EReal) (F : E → E) (ϕ lamBar : ℝ)
    (z zbar : ℕ → E) (lam theta : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hS : (solutionSet g F).Nonempty) (hg : IsProperConvexLSC g) (hF : IsMonotoneOnDom g F)
    (hL : IsLipschitzOnBoundedDom g F)
    (hrun : IsEGRAALRun g F ϕ lamBar z zbar lam theta) :
    ∃ zs ∈ solutionSet g F, Tendsto z atTop (𝓝 zs) ∧ Tendsto zbar atTop (𝓝 zs) := by sorry

end GoldenRatioVI.Explicit
